  <h1>Lesson 32: Form Validation - Check Before Sending</h1>
  <p>Name Empty? Email Valid? Password Strong? | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Test - 100 Marks</button>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Test is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the test or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is Form Validation?</h2>
    <p><b>Form Validation = Checking the form before sending it.</b> Is the name empty? Is the email valid? Is the password too short? Do the two passwords match?</p>
    <p>Without validation, users can send empty forms, wrong emails, or 1-letter passwords. With validation, you stop them and show a clear error message.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Real Life Example:</b> At an airport, security checks your ticket and ID before you board the plane. Form validation is the same - Check everything before you let the data go.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Signup Form With Validation</h2>
    <p>Try to submit with empty fields, wrong email, short password. See errors live:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <h3 id="formResult" style="margin:0">Create Your Account 📝</h3>
      <input class="demo-input" id="vName" type="text" placeholder="Full Name - e.g. Ali Ahmed" oninput="validateName()">
      <span class="err" id="nameErr"></span>
      <input class="demo-input" id="vEmail" type="text" placeholder="Email - e.g. ali@gmail.com" oninput="validateEmail()">
      <span class="err" id="emailErr"></span>
      <input class="demo-input" id="vPass" type="password" placeholder="Password - Min 6 characters" oninput="validatePass()">
      <div class="strength"><div class="strength-bar" id="passBar"></div></div>
      <span class="err" id="passErr"></span>
      <input class="demo-input" id="vConfirm" type="password" placeholder="Confirm Password - Same as above" oninput="validateConfirm()">
      <span class="err" id="confirmErr"></span>
      <button class="btn btn-js" style="width:100%" onclick="submitForm()">Create Account ✅</button>
      <button class="btn" onclick="resetForm()">Reset ↺</button>
    </div>
    <h2>3. Common Checks - Full Table</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Check</th><th>Code</th><th>Example</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Empty?</td><td>value === "" or value.trim() === ""</td><td>If name is empty, show "Name is required"</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Too Short?</td><td>value.length &lt; 6</td><td>Password must be at least 6 characters</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Too Long?</td><td>value.length &gt; 20</td><td>Username must be less than 20 characters</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Has @ ?</td><td>email.includes("@") && email.includes(".")</td><td>Email must have @ and .</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Passwords Match?</td><td>pass === confirmPass</td><td>Both passwords must be same</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Only Numbers?</td><td>!isNaN(value)</td><td>Phone must be numbers only</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Is Number?</td><td>age &gt;= 18</td><td>Age must be 18 or more</td></tr>
    </table>
    <h2>4. Basic Validation - Name Check</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function checkName() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let name = document.getElementById("name").value.trim();</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (name === "") {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("nameErr").innerText = "❌ Name is required!";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">return false; // Stop - Do not submit</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (name.length < 3) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("nameErr").innerText = "❌ Name must be at least 3 letters!";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">return false;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("nameErr").innerText = "✅ Good!";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">return true; // OK - Can submit</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>5. Email Validation</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function checkEmail() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let email = document.getElementById("email").value.trim();</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (email === "") {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">return "Email is required!";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (!email.includes("@") || !email.includes(".")) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">return "Invalid Email! Must have @ and .";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (email.indexOf("@") > email.lastIndexOf(".")) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">return "Invalid! . must come after @";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">return "Valid Email!";</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <p><b>Example:</b> <code>ali@gmail.com</code> ✅ - Has @ and . , . is after @.<br><code>aligmail.com</code> ❌ - No @.<br><code>ali@gmailcom</code> ❌ - No .</p>
    <h2>6. Password Validation + Strength</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function checkPassword() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let pass = document.getElementById("pass").value;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (pass.length < 6) { return "Password too short! Min 6 characters."; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (pass.length >= 6 && pass.length < 10) { return "Medium Password"; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (pass.length >= 10) { return "Strong Password!"; }</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Confirm Password - Must match</span><br>
<span class="text">let pass = document.getElementById("pass").value;</span><br>
<span class="text">let confirm = document.getElementById("confirm").value;</span><br>
<span class="text">if (pass !== confirm) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">alert("Passwords do not match!");</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>7. Complete Example - Full Form Check on Submit</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;form</span> <span class="attr">onsubmit</span>=<span class="val">"return validateForm()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"name"</span> <span class="attr">placeholder</span>=<span class="val">"Name"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"email"</span> <span class="attr">placeholder</span>=<span class="val">"Email"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button&gt;</span><span class="text">Submit</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/form&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="text">function validateForm() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let name = document.getElementById("name").value.trim();</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let email = document.getElementById("email").value.trim();</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (name === "") { alert("Name is required!"); return false; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (!email.includes("@")) { alert("Invalid Email!"); return false; }</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">alert("Form Submitted Successfully!");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">return true; // Allow submit</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Key Trick:</b> In <code>onsubmit="return validateForm()"</code>, if the function returns <b>false</b>, the form will NOT submit. If it returns <b>true</b>, the form WILL submit. This is how you stop a bad form.</div>
    <h2>8. Common Mistakes</h2>
    <p>1. <b>Forgetting trim():</b> User types only spaces "   " - Without trim(), your code thinks it is not empty. Always use <code>.trim()</code>.<br>2. <b>Forgetting return false:</b> You show the error, but the form still submits. Always return false on error.<br>3. <b>Checking only on submit:</b> Best practice is to check on <code>oninput</code> (live) + on submit (final check). Users get instant feedback.</p>
    <h2>9. Homework</h2>
    <p>In Playground, build this:</p>
    <p>1. Login form - Email + Password. If email has no @, show error. If password length &lt; 6, show error<br>2. Signup form - Name, Email, Password, Confirm Password. All 4 checks like demo<br>3. Phone check - Input must be 11 digits and numbers only. Hint: <code>phone.length === 11 && !isNaN(phone)</code></p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Validation = Check before sending | Empty = value.trim() === "" | Email = Must have @ and . , . after @ | Password = Min 6, check length | Match = pass === confirmPass | return false = Stop submit | return true = Allow submit | oninput = Live check, onsubmit = Final check | Always use trim() to remove spaces</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> <a href="/lesson33">Lesson 33 - LocalStorage</a> - Learn how to save data in the browser. Even after refresh, data stays.</p>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
