      <div id="quizArea">
        <form id="quizForm">
          <div class="question"><b>Q1. What is Form Validation?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> Checking form before sending - Name, email, password</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> Adding color to form</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> Adding image to form</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="d"> Deleting form</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q2. How to check if name is empty?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> name.trim() === ""</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> name === 0</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> name.length === 100</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="d"> name === null only</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q3. Valid email must have?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> @ and . , . after @</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> Only @</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> Only .</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="d"> Nothing</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q4. How to check passwords match?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="a"> pass === confirmPass</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="b"> pass = confirmPass</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="c"> pass > confirmPass</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="d"> pass + confirmPass</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q5. What does return false do in onsubmit?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="a"> Stops form from submitting</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="b"> Submits form</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="c"> Deletes form</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="d"> Nothing</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q6. What does return true do in onsubmit?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="a"> Allows form to submit</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="b"> Stops form</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="c"> Deletes form</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="d"> Nothing</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q7. Why use trim()?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="a"> To remove spaces - So "   " is treated as empty</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="b"> To add color</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="c"> To make uppercase</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="d"> To delete input</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q8. Password length is 4. What should happen if min is 6?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="a"> Show error - Too short</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="b"> Accept it</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="c"> Show success</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="d"> Nothing</label></div>
